[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118724,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Acute myeloid leukaemia (AML) with <em>CEBPA</em> mutation is characterized by <em>CEBPA</em> mutation that should be biallelic (bi<em>CEBPA</em>) or, if single, must be located in the bZIP region of the gene (smbZIP-<em>CEBPA</em>).</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118725,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9878/3 Acute myeloid leukaemia with <em>CEBPA</em> mutation</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118726,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2A60.0 &amp; XH4M02 Acute myeloid leukaemia with recurrent genetic abnormalities &amp; Acute myeloid leukaemia with biallelic mutation of <em>CEBPA</em></p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118727,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> acute myeloid leukaemia with biallelic mutation of <em>CEBPA</em>.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118728,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118729,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Blood and bone marrow</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118730,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Presenting symptoms and signs are typically secondary to bone marrow failure and include fatigue, bruising or bleeding, and infection. Patients with bi<em>CEBPA</em> and smbZIP-<em>CEBPA</em> are younger and have higher white blood cell counts than those with a single mutation in the N-terminal transactivation domain (TAD) {34320176}. Detection of bi<em>CEBPA</em> should raise suspicion of a germline <em>CEBPA</em> variant and referral for genetic counselling (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/28\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Myeloid neoplasms associated with germline predisposition</em>).</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118731,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>AML with <em>CEBPA</em> mutation constitutes approximately 5% of AML cases in children and 5&ndash;11% of AML cases in adults {33951732; 34320176; 34448807}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118732,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Among cases with bi<em>CEBPA</em>, approximately 5&ndash;10% have a germline N-terminal mutation {21177436}. In the familial form, AML has very high penetrance and presents relatively early (median age: 24.5&nbsp;years) {26162409}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118733,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The gene <em>CEBPA</em> encodes for a bZIP transcription factor that is essential for myeloid lineage commitment and regulates myeloid differentiation and stem/progenitor cell function {28179278}. The bZIP region is required for dimerization and DNA binding of this protein {15122210; 15674366}. The protein can interact with CDK2 and CDK4. Mutations can be biallelic or monoallelic (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/63/346/30053\" target=\"_blank\">#30053</a>Table&nbsp;2.16).</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118734,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118735,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Smear preparations show increased blasts with or without maturation {20038735; 20439648; 21134981; 34320176}. Dysplasia is common, especially dysgranulopoiesis and dysmegakaryopoiesis {22442349}.</p>\r\n<p>The leukaemic cells are often positive for CD7, CD13, CD15, CD33, CD34, and HLA-DR, but they rarely express CD56 or CD14 {15746035}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118736,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>See above.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118737,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>CEBPA</em> mutation can be defined by various molecular techniques (including PCR with fragment analysis and next-generation sequencing) that appropriately interrogate the <em>CEBPA</em> gene for mutation location.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118738,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> &ge;&nbsp;20% blasts with a myeloid immunophenotype in the bone marrow or blood; presence of biallelic mutations in <em>CEBPA</em>, or a single mutation located in the bZIP region; absence of criteria allowing for classification into other AMLs with defining genetic abnormalities; not fulfilling diagnostic criteria for myeloid neoplasm post cytotoxic therapy.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118739,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 118740,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The prognostic impact of different <em>CEBPA</em> mutations is shown in <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/63/346/30053\" target=\"_blank\">#30053</a>Table&nbsp;2.16 . bi<em>CEBPA</em> was previously required for this AML subtype because of the association with a favourable prognosis {19171880; 20038735; 20439648}. A similarly favourable prognosis has recently been shown for smbZIP-<em>CEBPA</em> in cohorts of children and adults aged up to 70&nbsp;years {33951732; 34320176; 34448807}, justifying the inclusion of this additional <em>CEBPA</em> mutation subset.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T12:37:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]